course: dictionary
lesson: 6403
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is meant. Muscat is a city and a grape. «The Gulf states include Oman (Muscat).» Oman is a country, so Muscat here must be the capital city of Oman.
explain: «Muscat grapes» are sweet grapes. The word grapes after muscat tells you it is the fruit. Ask: what word fits here? A city, or a kind of fruit? Then try your choice in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters help too. Muscat with a capital M is the city, and muscat with a small m is the grape. When you are not sure, check the clues around the word, as you would for any new word.
fact: Muscat is the capital city of Oman, a country on the Arabian Peninsula.
fact: Muscat is on the Gulf of Oman, and it was once an important port for sea trade with India and East Africa.
fact: A muscat is a kind of sweet grape with a musky, flowery flavour.
fact: Muscat grapes are eaten fresh, dried into raisins, or made into sweet wine.
fact: Muscat grapes are among the oldest grape varieties, so they have been grown for a very long time.
exercise: «The Gulf states include Oman (Muscat).» What is Muscat in this sentence? | A sea | A kind of fruit | A country | *A city
exercise: «The shop sold sweet muscat grapes.» What is muscat in this sentence? | *A kind of sweet grape | A type of boat | A city in Oman | A desert
exercise: Which city is the capital of Oman? | Dubai | Doha | *Muscat | Abu Dhabi
test: «Muscat, Oman» names a city. Which country is it in? | *Oman | Bahrain | Kuwait | Qatar
test: Muscat grapes can be eaten, dried or made into wine. What flavour do they have? | *Musky, flowery and sweet | Spicy, like pepper | Salty and sour | Bitter, like strong coffee
exam: In «The Gulf states include Oman (Muscat).», how can you tell Muscat is a city and not a grape? | Because it has more than five letters | *Because it names the capital of a country, and it has a capital M | Because grapes never grow near the sea | Because Oman is a kind of fruit
